{"java":{"id":"ad44e43b-dac0-45dc-a35f-4edb3b931fe2","word":"Java","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"island of Indonesia","tags":["feminine"],"word":"Java"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"programming language","tags":["masculine"],"word":"Java"}],"pos":"name","tags":null,"senses":[{"categories":["en:Islands","en:Places in Indonesia"],"links":[["island","island"],["Indonesia","Indonesia#English"]],"glosses":["An island in the Indonesian Archipelago, Indonesia."],"id":"e05e9338-ac4a-4463-aa48-9a46b2372a90"},{"examples":[{"text":"The awesome power of RSS delivered to me this morning a link to a new blog post by Robert X Cringeley. The post, The second coming of Java got me thinking.","ref":"2011 October 17, Matthew Baxter-Reynolds, “Java's second coming? Over my cold, dead RAM-cached database”, in The Guardian, archived from the original on 27 Jun 2022:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[134,138]],"id":"68455fda-e13f-477c-84b4-5eb04cde3f72"}],"topics":["computer-languages","computing","engineering","mathematics","natural-sciences","physical-sciences","sciences"],"senseid":["en:computer language"],"categories":["English terms with quotations","en:Computer languages"],"links":[["computer language","computer language"],["object-oriented","object-oriented"],["garbage-collected","garbage collection"],["programming language","programming language"]],"raw_glosses":["(computer languages) An object-oriented, garbage-collected computer programming language."],"glosses":["An object-oriented, garbage-collected computer programming language."],"id":"99caa61c-c3a4-4066-ab5c-fe099ed1c5a8"},{"examples":[{"ref":"1996 October 6, Timothy Litwiller, “HOW TO MAKE A JAVA ALERT POP UP ON LOAD”, in comp.lang.javascript (Usenet):","type":"quotation","id":"35aae5bc-8290-4aed-83f9-32aa28420995"},{"text":"In the input tag I include the onBlur=\"myfunction()\" which checks if the field is filled (displays an alert if necessary and resets the focus). If I leave the first field I get an java alert which says that field two should have a value and then a java alert which says that field one should have a value and then a java... get the picture ?","ref":"1996 December 10, Cédric Bouckaert, “onBlur event handler with input fields”, in comp.lang.javascript (Usenet):","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[180,184],[248,252],[316,320]],"id":"76c1da42-c4ac-4ef4-8e1b-b8916e19d5ec"},{"ref":"1997 January 7, Kenneth Roddy, “Java Alert Messages When Netscape Home Page Loads”, in comp.infosystems.www.browsers.ms-windows (Usenet):","type":"quotation","id":"3ae324be-8cbe-4294-8013-c741834fb838"},{"text":"I created an alert window using java script, but I found the fonts too small. Is there a way of controling font size and style when java alert window opens.","ref":"1997 February 18, AG, “alert...is there a way of controling font size and style when java alert window opens”, in comp.lang.javascript (Usenet):","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[32,36],[132,136]],"id":"b094668a-be03-482e-b0a5-58f016332a34"},{"ref":"2003 April 8, mpaulopes, “Passing values to a Java popup windows”, in macromedia.coldfusion.cfml_general_discussion (Usenet):","type":"quotation","id":"042e921f-de42-471f-b9b0-674b532182a4"}],"topics":["computer-languages","computing","engineering","mathematics","natural-sciences","physical-sciences","sciences"],"categories":["English proscribed terms","English terms with quotations","en:Computer languages"],"links":[["computer language","computer language"],["JavaScript","JavaScript"]],"raw_glosses":["(computer languages, proscribed) JavaScript (by confusion with Java)."],"glosses":["JavaScript (by confusion with Java)."],"tags":["proscribed"],"id":"4ba46491-f0fb-4774-9e75-69f788d3ff34"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"javelin":{"id":"71e00f01-a23e-48c4-864e-06a4319442fe","word":"javelin","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"spear used as a weapon","word":"dardo"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"spear used in athletic competition","tags":["masculine"],"word":"dardo"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"And when Phinehas the sonne of Eleazar, the sonne of Aaron the Priest saw it, hee rose vp from amongst the Congregation, and tooke a iauelin in his hand. And he went after the man of Israel into the tent, and thrust both of them thorow, the man of Israel, and the woman, thorow her belly: So the plague was stayed from the children of Israel.","ref":"1611, The Holy Bible, […] (King James Version), London: […] Robert Barker, […], →OCLC, Numbers 25:7–8:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[133,140]],"id":"2d95df21-3e31-4053-a9be-75a2216b2758"},{"text":"Flies the javelin swifter to its mark, / Launched by the vigour of a Roman arm?","ref":"1712 (date written), [Joseph] Addison, Cato, a Tragedy. […], London: […] J[acob] Tonson, […], published 1713, →OCLC, Act I, scene iv, page 9:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[10,17]],"id":"6700fdeb-72e4-4ff5-b3f6-329d1353adf8"},{"text":"With what apprehensions we proceeded, ignorant at what moment we might be greeted by the javelin of some ambushed savage!","ref":"1846 February 26, Herman Melville, chapter X, in Narrative of a Four Months’ Residence among the Natives of a Valley of the Marquesas Islands; or, A Peep at Polynesian Life [Typee], London: John Murray, […], →OCLC, part I, page 73:","english":"Typee","type":"quotation","translation":"Typee","bold_text_offsets":[[89,96]],"id":"3a107135-da1a-414b-a558-d052ce666a17"},{"text":"As a lion or wild boar turns fiercely on the dogs and men that attack him, while these form a solid wall and shower their javelins as they face him—his courage is all undaunted, but his high spirit will be the death of him;[…]","ref":"1898, Homer, “Book XII”, in Samuel Butler, transl., The Iliad of Homer: Rendered into English Prose for the use of those who cannot read the original, London: Longmans, 